{"id": 29, "ts": 1780731417.1670558, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "agent_2", "message": "I agree with Agent\u202f3\u2019s assessment that Candidate\u202fC remains the strongest overall. The recent clarification that we have no concrete observations of Candidate\u202fA\u2019s operational reliability or stress\u2011resilience on long\u2011haul flights leaves a critical gap in the evidence for a role where those criteria are non\u2011negotiable. Moreover, A\u2019s noted unorganized behaviour and resistance to criticism further weaken his reliability profile. Candidate\u202fB, while very conscientious and stress\u2011resilient, has been described as uncooperative and grumpy, which directly jeopardises crew\u2011cooperation and professional communication\u2014key safety\u2011critical factors. Candidate\u202fD shows solid problem\u2011solving and responsibility, but his hot temper and know\u2011it\u2011all attitude raise serious concerns about stress resilience and cockpit harmony. In contrast, Candidate\u202fC is documented as 100\u202f% reliable, creates a positive crew atmosphere, makes correct decisions quickly, and stays calm in crises, covering the core safety criteria. The only remaining reservations are his communication style and limited eagerness for further education, which, while not ideal, appear less hazardous than the cooperation deficits seen in B or the temper issues in D. Therefore, I maintain my vote for **Candidate\u202fC** as the best fit for the long\u2011distance pilot position."}
